The '''Minister of Innovation''' is a cabinet-level position in the [[Government of Burawa]], responsible for technology policy, digital government services, and research and development investment. The position was created in 1997 as part of a government reorganisation that elevated technology policy to a cabinet-level concern.

The minister heads the [[Ministry of Innovation (Burawa)|Ministry of Innovation]], which oversees e-government initiatives, technology education programmes, and government investment in technology startups.

